Third-party models in the model viewer
======================================

The globe keeps All Eyes' original green silhouettes. The top-right model viewer
loads the files below the first time that shape is shown. Airline liveries are
not included. Families without a row here are original procedural models in
src/ui/studio-models.ts, © All Eyes contributors, MIT, same terms as this
repository (https://github.com/rizxe134/All-Eyes).

Aircraft by amvlab
------------------

Author: amorfinv (amvlab)
Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
Source: https://github.com/amvlab/aircraft-models
Files used (the `*_nologo` builds, renamed):

| Viewer id | File                | Upstream model                          |
| --------- | ------------------- | --------------------------------------- |
| air-a320  | public/models/air-a320.glb | A320_nologo.glb                  |
| air-b737  | public/models/air-b737.glb | B737_nologo.glb                  |
| air-a350  | public/models/air-a350.glb | A350_nologo.glb                  |
| air-b777  | public/models/air-b777.glb | B787_nologo.glb                  |
| air-a380  | public/models/air-a380.glb | A380_nologo.glb                  |

The Boeing widebody-twin family (777 and 787) shares one sprite. The mesh in
the viewer is the 787, not a 777. Changes: none to the geometry; the files are
served as glTF binary and shown with this app's lighting.

Credit required by CC BY: "A320 / 737 / A350 / 787 / A380 model by amvlab"
(the viewer credit line links the repository and the licence).

NASA 3D Resources
-----------------

Author: NASA
Licence: Public domain (United States government work)
Source: https://github.com/nasa/NASA-3D-Resources
https://nasa3d.arc.nasa.gov/

| Viewer id    | File                       | Upstream model              |
| ------------ | -------------------------- | --------------------------- |
| air-heli     | public/models/air-heli.glb     | Ingenuity Mars Helicopter |
| sat-wx       | public/models/sat-wx.glb       | Aqua                      |
| sat-nav      | public/models/sat-nav.glb      | CYGNSS                    |
| sat-science  | public/models/sat-science.glb  | CubeSat 1RU Generic       |

The ISS mesh published by NASA is too large for this app. The station in the
viewer is an original procedural model, not that file. Ingenuity is a coaxial
Mars helicopter; it stands in for the helicopter family.

These NASA files use Draco mesh compression and, where noted upstream, WebP
textures. They are decoded in the browser. They were not otherwise modified.

Draco decoder
-------------

public/draco/gltf/draco_decoder.wasm
public/draco/gltf/draco_wasm_wrapper.js

Author: Google
Licence: Apache License 2.0
https://github.com/google/draco
Copied from the three.js r170 examples (examples/jsm/libs/draco/gltf/), which
redistribute the decoder. Loaded only when a compressed model is opened.

Procedural stand-ins
--------------------

Built in code when no suitable small CC0 or CC-BY model was found. Original
work, MIT, All Eyes contributors:

- air-b747, air-rj, air-prop, air-light, air-fighter, air-biz, air-cargo, air-unk
- ship-cargo, ship-tanker, ship-pax, ship-fish, ship-mil, ship-tug, ship-sail, ship-unk
- sat-station, sat-comms, sat-debris
- weather and abstract markers (storm, quake, launch, fire, volcano, and the plain marker)

Not used
--------

Flightradar24 models and other tracker assets are not included.
